.TH HEE-STATUS 7 "2026-09-01" "HEE" "Overviews and Conventions"
.SH NAME
hee-status \- the org's status vocabulary and exit-code convention
.SH DESCRIPTION
One vocabulary across every HEE tool, adopted from the Nagios plugin API
rather than invented:
.PP
.TS
l l l.
Level	Exit	Meaning
OK	0	the thing checked is correct
WARNING	1	real but non-blocking
CRITICAL	2	blocking; the check has failed
UNKNOWN	3	the check could not run
.TE
.PP
.B UNKNOWN is not a failure.
It means the check did not produce a result \(em an unreachable host, a
missing interpreter. Reporting that as OK or CRITICAL is the error this
level exists to prevent.
.SH ICON AND LABEL, NEVER COLOUR ALONE
Every line ships an icon
.I and
a text label. Icons are shape\-distinct (check, triangle, cross, question)
rather than hue\-only, so they survive colour blindness, a monochrome pipe,
and a log file.
.PP
.B Machine consumers parse the label, never the icon.
Decoupled 2026\-08\-31 so presentation can change without breaking parsers.
.SH STYLES
.TP
.B icon
Default. Icon plus label.
.TP
.B ascii
Bracketed label, no emoji \(em for pipes, logs and terminals without font
coverage.
.TP
.B plain
Label and message only.
.PP
Selected with
.B HEE_STATUS_STYLE
\(em see
.BR heerc (5).
Preview with
.BR "hee_status_demo" .
